WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.347
Too many questions, too many documents, and not enough
time?

00:00:04.347 --> 00:00:09.564
This is Elevate for Humanity, and I am PARIS, your AI
presenter.

00:00:09.564 --> 00:00:13.041
Today, meet the assistants described in Elevate's store.

00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:15.650
PARIS focuses on sales and intake.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:18.258
ELLIE focuses on learning and support.

00:00:18.258 --> 00:00:19.997
LIZZY focuses on operations.

00:00:19.997 --> 00:00:22.170
ZORA focuses on compliance assistance.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.648
Think of a training organization receiving an inquiry.

00:00:25.648 --> 00:00:29.126
Intake guidance can help organize the person's
questions.

00:00:29.126 --> 00:00:33.473
Learning support can point a learner toward relevant
course information.

00:00:33.473 --> 00:00:37.820
Operations assistance can help staff organize documents
and next steps.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:43.036
Compliance assistance can help prepare material for a
qualified human to review.

00:00:43.036 --> 00:00:49.122
These are examples of how to use the tools, not a claim
that every

00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:50.426
task happens automatically.

00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:55.643
AI does not decide grant eligibility, award licenses, or
replace professional judgment.

00:00:55.643 --> 00:01:00.425
Use approved materials, protect private information, and
check outputs before acting.

00:01:00.425 --> 00:01:06.511
Choose one repetitive task this week, write down its
current steps, and test whether

00:01:06.511 --> 00:01:09.119
an assistant makes the work clearer.

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:12.162
Compare the result against your normal process.

00:01:12.162 --> 00:01:17.813
Visit the store to inspect the assistants, their current
prices, and their limits.

00:01:17.813 --> 00:01:20.856
Follow the show for more practical demonstrations.

